# Unlike the upstream template (which ignores lockfiles since the CLI
# supports npm/yarn/pnpm interchangeably), this submission keeps
# package-lock.json committed deliberately -- it's proof `npm install` was
# run for real against the real npm registry, same convention this
# session's tray-anakin submission used for the same reason.
